+# Local RoboTwin v0 evaluation plan — 2026-10-30
+
+User requests this exact RoboTwin checkpoint evaluated as FastWAM, carefully and efficiently. Use an isolated worktree based on the release loader branch; preserve previous LIBERO reports and cancellations.
+
+1. Pin HF revision and verify all nine release files by size/SHA or Git blob. Strict-load original v0 epoch5,14D,4/4,step237310; confirm stats and VAE hashes.
+2. Install SAPIEN3.0.0b1/MPLib0.2.1/CuRobo0.7.8 in a separate environment with existing PyTorch2.7.1+cu128. Download and verify pinned official RoboTwin assets; restore task_config from vendor's exact upstream commit.
+3. Use released FastWAM scene harness and preprocessing (PIL resize uint8 and BF16 normalization), RT32samples/depth8/OIDN; no H100 raster fallback. Record preprocessing change versus release's training-native evaluator. Keep native LoopWAM FP32weights/BF16 inference.
+4. Seed42 scene start4300000; all50tasks; clean and randomized;100acceptedepisodes per cell; unseen templates;32actions/execute24;NFE10/CFG1. Preserve original expert acceptance. No explicit Python instruction reseeding unlike uploaded H100 run.
+5. Validate real renderer/expert/policy rollouts and videos. Enable CUDA graph only if bit-exact native comparisons pass on multiple real observations; otherwise eager fallback. Benchmark memory-safe concurrency; no protocol reduction for speed.
+6. Freeze runtime code, configuration, asset, weight and T5 identities. Queue100task/setting cells with bounded retries, validated completed-cell resume, no failed/crashed episodes counted as scored. Preserve videos/instructions/action traces, report per-task and setting results.
+7. Independent audit found shader, image transform, language RNG and provenance differences. Address before launch. Tests, smoke results and complete manifest are launch gates. Persistent tmux queue runs to completion; report measured ETA after sufficient completed cells.
